/* What the Linux band3 executable exports to the shared libraries it loads
   (CMakeLists.txt, through --version-script).

   The SDK's runtime library calls band3's overrides of its exports by name
   (__imp__*, src/sdk_export.cpp), and C++ inline functions and their guard
   variables (_Z*) are shared as the C++ rules ask. Nothing else: the
   recompiled guest functions keep the names band3_functions.toml gives them, and
   some are a C library's (the game's zlib: crc32, inflate, deflate...). An
   executable exports every definition a shared library could call, so Mesa's
   Vulkan drivers (crc32) and libcurl (inflate) called the game's PowerPC
   code in place of zlib's, and crashed. */
{
  global:
    __imp__*;
    _Z*;
  local:
    *;
};
